## clean site build — `rm -rf site/dist && npm run build` (site/)

`rm -rf site/dist` is load-bearing: the clean must be real or stale files survive.

The old `node:crypto` externalization warning must be ABSENT, paired with a positive
control on the SAME invocation (a real successful build log always prints `built in`):

    grep -c 'externalized for browser compatibility' <build log>   -> 0   (absent)
    grep -c 'built in'                        <build log>   -> 3   (control)

build exit=0; 8 pages built.

